  "topicTitle": "Using a calculator",
  "skills": {
    "Basic operations (+, -, ×, ÷, %, powers), and other functions including storing/recalling values, exact/approx modes, and reset to default.": {
      "items": [
        {
          "q": "Evaluate: (3.5 + 2.7) × 4",
          "a": "24.8",
          "hints": [
            "Do the bracket first, then multiply.",
            "3.5 + 2.7 = 6.2, so calculate 6.2 × 4.",
            "(3.5 + 2.7) × 4 = 6.2 × 4 = 24.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "q": "Evaluate: 7.2^2",
          "a": "51.84",
          "hints": [
            "Use the x² (square) key, or multiply the number by itself.",
            "7.2 × 7.2.",
            "7.2^2 = 7.2 × 7.2 = 51.84"
          ]
        },
        {
          "q": "Evaluate: sqrt(196) + 1/4",
          "a": "14.25",
          "hints": [
            "Work out the square root and the fraction separately, then add.",
            "sqrt(196) = 14, and 1/4 = 0.25.",
            "sqrt(196) + 1/4 = 14 + 0.25 = 14.25"
          ]
        },
        {
          "q": "Evaluate: 18% of 250",
          "a": "45",
          "hints": [
            "Turn the percentage into a decimal, then multiply.",
            "18% = 0.18, so calculate 250 × 0.18.",
            "18% of 250 = 0.18 × 250 = 45"
          ]
        },
        {
          "q": "Evaluate: (5.6 - 1.8) ÷ 0.2",
          "a": "19",
          "hints": [
            "Do the bracket first, then divide.",
            "5.6 - 1.8 = 3.8, so calculate 3.8 ÷ 0.2.",
            "(5.6 - 1.8) ÷ 0.2 = 3.8 ÷ 0.2 = 19"
          ]
        },
        {
          "q": "Evaluate: 3^4 - 2^5",
          "a": "49",
          "hints": [
            "Work out each power separately before subtracting.",
            "3^4 = 81, and 2^5 = 32.",
            "3^4 - 2^5 = 81 - 32 = 49"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
